From afd8a247e769893b2ac97a15f41af71e6e6ab4a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majed Alkhaleefah <majed@freebsd.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:24:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] bthid: Add Bluetooth HID bus driver and hidbus transport
 driver

Add a new kernel transport driver (bthid) and a bus driver (bthidbus)
to interface Bluetooth HID devices directly with the hid subsystem.

bthidbus exposes a character device interface to allow userland processes
to pass established sockets and device info to the kernel via ioctl.
bthid attaches to bthidbus as a child device, routing incoming HID reports
from the interrupt socket into hidbus.

Connection establishment (pairing, SDP querying) is handled entirely in
userland; this driver only takes ownership of already-connected sockets.
